{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "id": "poly.quadratic",
      "label": "Quadratic polynomial",
      "subject": "maths",
      "level": "class-10",
      "definition": "A polynomial of degree two, written a x squared plus b x plus c with a not zero.",
      "prerequisites": [
        "alg.equation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "poly.zero",
      "label": "Zero of a polynomial",
      "subject": "maths",
      "level": "class-10",
      "definition": "A number that makes the value of the polynomial zero when it is put in place of x.",
      "prerequisites": [
        "poly.quadratic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "poly.zeroes.relation",
      "label": "Sum and product of the zeroes",
      "subject": "maths",
      "level": "class-10",
      "definition": "For a x squared plus b x plus c the zeroes add up to minus b over a and multiply to c over a.",
      "prerequisites": [
        "poly.zero"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "kb.own.maths10.poly",
      "title": "Notes on zeroes of a quadratic polynomial (written by the project in its own words; the school book is cited as a pointer, not copied)",
      "rightsHolder": "LearningUplift project",
      "licence": "owner-original",
      "passages": [
        {
          "id": "p1",
          "loc": "notes 1",
          "text": "A polynomial of degree two is called a quadratic polynomial. It can be written as a x squared plus b x plus c, where a, b and c are real numbers and a is not zero."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "loc": "notes 2",
          "text": "A zero of a polynomial is a number which, put in place of x, makes the value of the polynomial zero. On the graph a zero is a point where the curve meets the x axis."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "loc": "notes 3",
          "text": "If the zeroes of a x squared plus b x plus c are alpha and beta, then alpha plus beta equals minus b divided by a, and alpha times beta equals c divided by a."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "loc": "notes 4",
          "text": "For two x squared minus eight x plus six the zeroes are one and three. Their sum, four, is eight divided by two, which is minus b divided by a, and their product, three, is six divided by two, which is c divided by a."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5",
          "loc": "notes 5",
          "text": "A common slip is to forget the minus sign and say that the sum of the zeroes is b divided by a. The sum of the zeroes is minus b divided by a."
        },
        {
          "id": "p6",
          "loc": "notes 6",
          "text": "A quadratic polynomial has at most two zeroes."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
